pe":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"C088\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"The answer splits the fees as required. It says the fixed fee covers standardized processing such as transfer agent and custody settlement. It says the variable fee covers commissions, taxes, spreads and market impact of trading basket securities to avoid diluting remaining shareholders.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"The answer says the AP pays both fees, which is the core of the point. It does not say the fee may be waived or paid by another party. It does not say recipients can differ between service provider and fund. Instead it says all transaction fees go to the fund.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"The answer states that fund charges and AP compensation are distinct. It calls the transaction fee cost recovery owed to the fund and describes AP compensation (arbitrage profit, dealer fees) as the AP's own economics. Waiver frequency is optional.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":\"\\\"Transaction fees go to the fund to offset its costs... Service providers are paid from fund expenses, though fees may be routed through them operationally.\\\" This presents the fund as the universal recipient. That contradicts the supplied evidence that fixed charges can go directly to the custodian or another service provider. It is a material ancillary falsehood about recipients, which caps the grade at partial.\",\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"There is no central error, because the answer never says the fund's charge compensates the AP. Required coverage is 2.5 of 3. However, the claim that all transaction fees go to the fund, with providers paid from fund expenses, misstates the recipient structure. It also omits the waiver and third-party payment caveat. The material local falsehood caps the grade at partial.\"}","ttft_ms":4605,"type":"result","duration_ms":9006,"uuid":"e5b1bab3-11de-43b2-9ea2-50d9c06b54fc","ttft_stream_ms":1081,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":1081,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
